.TH AVR\-SERVICE\-TOKEN\-SET\-ACCESS 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-service-token-set-access \- Replace a service token's whole access selection.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr service-token set-access
[OPTIONS] TOKEN_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace a service token's whole access selection.
.PP
The grants given here replace every grant the token holds: a grant you leave out is removed, so repeat the ones to keep. The VM create limit stays unless --vm-create-limit or --no-vm-create changes it. When the change removes or lowers a grant or the limit, the command lists what goes and asks first; without a terminal it then refuses unless --yes is given. It reads the token first and the change fails if the token changes in between. A grant that widens its access must be within your own access now. The API may ask for a recent sign-in; the command then exits 4 and says to sign in again. The change applies to the token's next request.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr service-token set-access <token-id> --repo acme/api --repo acme/web
    avr service-token set-access <token-id> --all-firewall-rules --yes
    avr service-token set-access <token-id> --repo acme/api --vm-create-limit 10
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fITOKEN_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR, \fB\-R\fR \fITEXT\fR
Grant read access to a repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-firewall\-rule\fR \fITEXT\fR
Grant read access to an egress firewall rule, by rule ID (efr-xxx). Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-firewall\-rules\fR
Grant read access to every egress firewall rule, including rules added later.
.TP
\fB\-\-vm\fR \fITEXT\fR
Grant access to a VM, by VM ID (cvm-xxx): read, or write with cvm-xxx:write. Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-vms\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Grant read or write access to every VM of the organization, including VMs created later. (choices: read, write)
.TP
\fB\-\-vm\-create\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Let the token create VMs while it owns fewer than this many. A token of the root group cannot have a limit. Lowering it keeps the VMs the token owns. Omit to keep the current limit.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-vm\-create\fR
Withdraw the token's permission to create VMs. It keeps administering the VMs it created.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Apply the change without asking, even when it removes or lowers access.
.SH SEE ALSO
